Z||000000||1FST2M6||01-08-2001||08:27 AM||||while Shaun41178 was at his 'rents house he contacted me saying he had stop in my home town but neglected to contact me.(from Daytona,Fl to Toledo-ish, OH) After much jeering and ranting.. he said "sorry.. i'll call ya this time.." expecting him around 3am  i warned my Fiance to expect a phone call... well when the Alarm clock went off at 6:30 i was kinda bummed... thinking shaun didn't call.. but Just as we were walking out the door to head to work. he calls.. I went and chatted with him and his friend for a little over an hour. We pointed an laughed at the lamenites in the Shopping cart handled Civics discussed what avenue to take with the intake/head he droped off and we split.  Really great guys in a JAM packed 85 GT.. that had to be a LOOONG ride.. thanks for calling this time! <P>Then after over a week of playing on the phone trying to get a REAL ASE mechanic to help me with Preditors car  he just towed it to the Shop... 8:15 saturday morning rolls around and i get to the shop.. and Donald an i hook up.. after a tour of the shop we dove in to his BEAUTIFUL 20,448 original mile 85 GT 4spd. after a little instruction from Ed we did a compression test... they varied  <P>         115  120  165<BR> (tranny)145  145  150<P>but once i pulled the compression fitting out of the back plug hole and saw it draing the coolant out we knew that there was some kinda head gasket issue and removed the decklid. laid it in the back of the shop and cleaned up so the master mechs can continue to fix it.  the Design One stage 2 kit Donald is running is a REALLY nice setup.. with a REALLY small turbo. once it's all apart well get pics and once it's together well have dyno numbers.. on button up and after tuning... thanks for your help Donald and i and i'm sure ed will keep you posted on it's progress.    <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
